      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Para entenderlo, volvamos al día en que nació.",
          "en": "To understand, we go back to the day he was born."
        },
        {
          "es": "El poeta Hesíodo cuenta que Hera lo tuvo sola, sin Zeus. Lo hizo por rabia, porque Zeus había creado a Atenea solo.",
          "en": "The poet Hesiod says Hera had him alone, without Zeus. She did it out of anger, because Zeus had made Athena alone."
        },
        {
          "es": "Hera quería un hijo perfecto, para demostrar que era tan fuerte como Zeus.",
          "en": "Hera wanted a perfect child, to prove she was as strong as Zeus."
        },
        {
          "es": "Pero el bebé era pequeño y débil, y sus piernas estaban torcidas.",
          "en": "But the baby was small and weak, and his legs were twisted."
        },
        {
          "es": "Hera miró a su hijo y sintió vergüenza. No quería que los otros dioses lo vieran.",
          "en": "Hera looked at her son and felt ashamed. She did not want the other gods to see him."
        }
